.TH YOUTUBEDL\-GUI 1 "September 2026" "youtubedl-gui 4.5.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
youtubedl\-gui \- graphical front end to yt\-dlp for downloading videos and audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B youtubedl\-gui
.RI [ Qt-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B youtubedl\-gui
is a simple graphical interface to
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
the command line program for downloading videos from a wide variety of
sites.
It presents a single window in which a URL is entered, a destination
folder chosen, and the desired output selected; the download is then
performed by
.B yt\-dlp
with post\-processing by
.BR ffmpeg (1).
.PP
Two modes of operation are offered, on separate tabs of the window.
In audio mode the video is downloaded and its sound track extracted,
with a choice of audio format and quality, and metadata embedded in the
resulting file.
In video mode the video itself is kept, with a choice of container
format and of maximum resolution, and the thumbnail and any subtitles
optionally embedded.
Whole playlists can be fetched rather than a single item.
.PP
Progress is shown while the download runs, and a download in progress
can be cancelled.
When the download finishes and the window is not the active one, a
desktop notification is emitted using
.BR notify\-send (1),
if it is available; otherwise a dialogue box reports the outcome.
.PP
Checking the
.B Defaults
box leaves the format and quality selections to the website and to
.BR yt\-dlp ,
and greys out the corresponding controls.
The settings in effect when the program exits, that box included, are
written to the configuration file described below and restored on the
next run.
.PP
The program takes no options of its own.
Arguments are passed to Qt, so the standard Qt and X11 options such as
.B \-style
and
.B \-\-platform
are accepted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_AUTO_SCREEN_SCALE_FACTOR
Set this to
.B 1
for the window to scale correctly on a HiDPI display under GNOME and
other GTK based desktops.
Qt based desktops such as KDE apply their own scaling factor and need
no such setting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ytdl\-gui/ytdl\-gui.conf
Settings saved when the program exits and restored when it starts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ytdl\-gui/yt\-dlp.path
If this file exists, its first line is used as the command to run
instead of searching for
.B yt\-dlp
on the
.BR PATH .
This is useful when a newer
.B yt\-dlp
than the packaged one is installed elsewhere, for instance under
.IR ~/.local/bin .
.TP
.I /tmp/ytdl_stderr
Standard error of the most recent
.B yt\-dlp
run, shown in the dialogue reporting a failed download.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR notify\-send (1)
.PP
The upstream home page is
.UR https://codeberg.org/impromptux/ytdl\-gui
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
.B youtubedl\-gui
was written by Jason Goulet\-Lipman and is now maintained by
Impromptux.
.PP
